# Development Workflow

Use Melos and the root Makefile. Prefer the narrowest validation that covers the touched area.

## Commands

- `melos exec --scope=<package> -- flutter analyze` — single package (preferred)
- `melos analyze` — whole workspace (multi-package changes only)
- `melos test:core` / `melos test:multichoice` / `melos test:all`
- `make db` — build_runner; `make fb` / `make frb` / `make mr` / `make clean`

## Code generation

Generated: `*.g.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`, `*.config.dart`, `*.auto_mappr.dart`, `*.gr.dart`, `*.mocks.dart`, `strings.g.dart` (slang). Do not hand-edit. Mocks: `packages/core/test/mocks.dart` → regenerate via Melos.

- i18n: edit `apps/multichoice/lib/i18n/*.i18n.json`, then `make slang` or `melos slang` (included in `make db` / `make fb`).

## Validation

1. Focused tests for the touched package.
2. Scoped analyze (`multichoice`, `core`, `ui_kit`, `models`, `theme`).
3. `melos analyze` / `melos test:all` for shared or cross-package changes.
4. Add/update tests for new behavior and bug fixes; fix introduced lints before finishing.
5. State skipped validation and remaining risk when blocked.
